abstract: Many services ask for an email address before they do anything else, and that address links a person to the records associated with the account. This paper describes an architecture in which authenticated DNS use establishes an enrolled relationship between a service and a device, so that settings, shared access, individual permissions, recovery and paid features work without a name, an email address or an account password.
